## 7. Page structure

A **single-page site** (no router needed). Sections, top to bottom:

1. **Hero / header**
   - Logo (large, centered)
   - Brand wordmark + tagline ("Abi Cocina" / "Sabores de Venezuela")
   - Short intro sentence in Spanish: *"Comida casera venezolana, hecha con amor por Abi Norma."*
   - "**Ver menú**" CTA that smooth-scrolls to the menu.
   - Subtle background: `bg-abi-mist` with a faint repeating heart pattern (optional, very low opacity).

2. **About strip** (one short paragraph)
   - 2–3 sentences in Spanish about Abi Norma, her family recipes, and her Venezuelan tradition.
   - Small photo placeholder (round, 200px) — leave a TODO comment for the family to add a real photo of Abi Norma later.

3. **Menu**
   - One section per category (Granos, Arepas, Pollo/Pavo/Pescado, Carnes).
   - Category header: emoji + name in Playfair Display, subtitle (e.g., *"Bandejas de 1 libra"*) below in small caps.
   - **Item card grid** (2 columns on mobile, 3 on tablet, 4 on desktop):
     - Square image at top (rounded corners, object-cover)
     - Spanish name (bold)
     - English name (smaller, italic, abi-deep/60)
     - Portion size (e.g., "1 lb") as a small pill badge
     - Quantity stepper: `−  0  +` (only shows + button until count > 0, then shows the full stepper)
   - When any item has quantity ≥ 1, a **sticky bottom bar** slides up with:
     - "X artículos en tu pedido" + total item count
     - Big light-blue "**Hacer pedido por WhatsApp**" button

4. **Footer**
   - Logo small
   - "Síguenos" + (placeholder) Instagram / Facebook icons → leave `href="#"` with a TODO
   - WhatsApp icon → link to `https://wa.me/<phone>` (no pre-filled message, just opens chat)
   - Service area: "Houston · Katy · alrededores"
   - Small line: "Cocina por Abi Norma"
   - © 2026 Abi Cocina

## 8. WhatsApp integration (the only "logic")

When the user taps "Hacer pedido por WhatsApp":

```js
// src/lib/whatsapp.js
export function buildWhatsAppUrl(phone, cart, categories) {
  // Flatten cart items with their info, preserving menu order
  const lines = [];
  for (const cat of categories) {
    const catItems = cat.items
      .map(item => ({ ...item, qty: cart[item.id] || 0 }))
      .filter(item => item.qty > 0);
    if (catItems.length === 0) continue;
    lines.push(`*${cat.name}*`);
    for (const item of catItems) {
      lines.push(`• ${item.qty}× ${item.name} (${item.portion})`);
    }
    lines.push(''); // blank line between categories
  }

  const totalItems = Object.values(cart).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);

  const message =
`¡Hola Abi Norma! 🇻🇪

Me gustaría hacer el siguiente pedido:

${lines.join('\n').trim()}

Total: ${totalItems} ${totalItems === 1 ? 'artículo' : 'artículos'}.

¿Me confirmas disponibilidad y precio total? ¡Gracias!`;

  return `https://wa.me/${phone}?text=${encodeURIComponent(message)}`;
}
```

**Behavior on click:**
- Open the URL with `window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener,noreferrer')`.
- Do **not** clear the cart afterward — the user might come back to adjust.
- On mobile, this opens the WhatsApp app directly. On desktop, WhatsApp Web.

