- [ ] `README.md` clearly tells the grandchild **(a) where to put Abi Norma's phone number, (b) how to swap images, and (c) how to edit menu items**.

## 12. Deployment to Netlify

Add a `netlify.toml` at the project root:

```toml
[build]
  command  = "npm run build"
  publish  = "dist"

[[redirects]]
  from   = "/*"
  to     = "/index.html"
  status = 200
```

Two ways to deploy — explain both in the README:

1. **Drag-and-drop:** run `npm run build`, then drag the `dist/` folder onto [app.netlify.com/drop](https://app.netlify.com/drop). Instant URL.
2. **Git-connected:** push to GitHub, "Add new site → Import" on Netlify, point at the repo. Auto-deploys on every push.

For a custom domain (e.g., `abicocina.com`), Netlify will walk through DNS — note this in the README as an optional upgrade.

